) that are missing.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer A recommends Marco Silva as the exposure reviewer, with Anna and Lena as backups, and presents them as active owners. It does not say that no active person is a real expert in exposure/. Its Kochnev count of 429 lines is below the 62-76% share range once totals are considered, and it does not say active people own at most 8%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A recommends Marco Silva and Lena Brandt for the delegator code, and says Lena has 10 surviving lines. The ground truth says nobody active owns any delegator lines. It does not say the active share is 0%. It names active owners, which is an explicit FAIL condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 143 surviving lines in exposure/ and recommends them as the owner. grouped_exposure.rb is credited to Marco instead of to Kochnev, who wrote the file it was copied from. It gives no repo-wide share for Marco and does not mention Anna's patch correctly.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A presents Lena Brandt as an active owner with 10 surviving lines, when the truth is 0 attributable lines. It gives no departed-share figure, and it says nothing about Peter Scholz or Andrey Subbota.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B says dblock has the most commits and Kochnev has the most lines, so the direction is right. Its numbers are off: dblock at 18.2% of commits and 10.4% of lines, against the required 28-36% and 3-8%. Kochnev is at 18.7% against the required 21-29%. Its figures come from a tool run without merging identities, which gives a commit share below 20%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B says the exposure owners have mostly left, but it credits Kochnev with only 54.4% of exposure/ and credits Marco Silva with 19.2%. It says active people hold 19.9%, against the truth of 2.6%. It recommends Marco Silva if confirmed, and flags the uncertainty, but its numbers are wrong.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B finds Kochnev owns 77% of delegators/ and that nobody there has committed in the last year, which matches the truth of 75% and 0% active. It lists Marco Silva with 4 lines in delegator.rb, which is not a large share. However, it handles delegator.rb separately and does not follow the history back as the criterion asks. It does not credit Marco with 10% or more of the delegator code and does not name an active owner of delegators/.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 117 lines, all in grouped_exposure.rb, and notes the two addresses without merging them. It does not trace the file to Kochnev, so grouped_exposure.rb is credited mostly to Marco. It gives no repo-wide share for Marco, and it does not mention Anna's patch correctly.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives no figure for the departed share, no Lena Brandt analysis, no dependabot, and nothing on Scholz versus Subbota. It also treats Peter Scholz as a separate name and lists him as inactive, which is correct, but that is not enough to meet the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Doubrovkine has about 119 commits with the identities merged, and that he is not among the top line owners. It names Kochnev as the largest owner who stopped in 2015. It gives no percentages, so it does not show the 31.8% commit share or the 5.6% line share, and it never says Kochnev is the top owner repo-wide.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C recommends Marco Silva as the exposure reviewer and lists Lena Brandt as active. It does not state that active people own at most 8% of exposure/. It credits Marco with the second-largest block of lines and lists him as a real fit, so it treats an active person as a real expert.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C recommends Lena Brandt as the first reviewer for delegators, and says she has 12 lines. This names an active person as an owner of the delegator code, when nobody active owns any of it. That is an explicit FAIL condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure/ and says he is the best fit. It does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev, does not give a repo-wide share, and does not mention Anna's patch.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C credits Lena Brandt with 18 exposure lines and 12 delegator lines, and presents her as an owner. This fails the 0-lines requirement. It gives no departed-share figure and does not discuss Scholz or Subbota.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C_note\": \"none\"}","ttft_ms":13837,"type":"result","duration_ms":13858,"uuid":"893d67ba-39f5-4ac5-abe5-ed673d8a3286","ttft_stream_ms":1871,"time_to_request_ms":486,"first_content_frame_ms":1871,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
